Dear Krasicki Family,

I wanted to provide an update on the restoration of your estate clock.
Work is progressing well. The movement has been fully disassembled,
cleaned, and inspected. The case has been stabilised and the first round
of conservation work on the woodwork is complete.

I have ordered the replacement parts from Stefan Muller in Biel,
Switzerland. Stefan is one of the finest precision parts suppliers in
Europe and I have worked with him for over fifteen years. The parts
include a new balance staff, mainspring set, and escapement wheel
components. The total parts budget remains confirmed at PLN 2,800 as
agreed in our original contract.

Stefan expects to complete quality assurance and ship by mid-October. I
am still targeting delivery of the restored clock to you by October 26,
2026. I will contact you again as the delivery date approaches to
arrange logistics.

Please do not hesitate to reach out if you have any questions.

With kind regards,
